From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:37:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: rtkit: wake a co-processor with its retained
 session

apple_rtkit_idle() leaves a co-processor's firmware, endpoints and shared
buffers in place, but waking it again goes through INIT and starts the
system endpoints anew. The J713 DCP is to stop its CPU after the idle
handshake, power its domains down and start the CPU again later. Its
firmware then says HELLO by itself, and macOS answers the endpoint map
with the endpoints that are still running, without INIT and without
starting any endpoint.

Add apple_rtkit_wake_retained(). From the idle state, with RX held by the
caller since the idle, it restores the mailbox (apple_mbox_restore(), as
its power domain may have been off), resumes RX and lets the caller start
the CPU. While it runs, the endpoint map is answered with the endpoints
started in this session, which RTKit now records, and nothing is started
again; a started endpoint missing from the map fails the wake. A
co-processor that first reports QUIESCED gets one ON request, any other
IOP state before ON fails the wake. The usual boot wait then requires IOP
ON and requests AP ON. Nothing is allocated, freed or reinitialized.

A signal to the caller does not interrupt the wake's waits: the CPU is
running by then, and nothing would undo that. An unexpected IOP state
ends whichever wait the wake is in, the map or IOP ON after it. A last
map part cannot echo endpoint 32 * base, as bit 0 of the reply is also
MORE: such a wake fails. The DCP's map has two parts, with its endpoint 0
in the first.

Also accept management message 0xc, which some co-processors send once
idle after the IOP IDLE request, instead of warning about it.

apple_mbox_restore() sets the mailbox-level enables of a started mailbox
again, as apple_mbox_start() does.

Host test: the retained endpoint map replies for the DCP's map, a missing
started endpoint, a last part that cannot be echoed, QUIESCED before ON,
an unexpected state before and after the map, the unchanged
acknowledgment outside a retained wake, and which waits a signal can
interrupt. The OSLog test's RTKit stub gains the started endpoint bitmap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit f5c0fe0da453e9f16e8564281766c026ac7c500b)
[j604: mailbox.c conflict resolved by hand: a15y lacks the Aurora ASCWrap v8 receive poller block in the context; only the apple_mbox_start -> apple_mbox_enable_hw split applied on the a15y body; tools/asahi/run-host-tests.py not carried on a15y, dropped]
